      "original_text": "/dso:brainstorm writes the `brainstorm:complete` tag on the epic at Phase 3 completion and removes any `scrutiny:pending` tag in the same `ticket edit --tags=` operation (read-merge-write pattern preserves other tags).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time tag operation performed at a specific phase milestone, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "sprint-list-epics.sh `--has-tag=<tag>` (net-new flag) returns only tickets carrying that tag; `_build_index()` includes each ticket's `tags` field. /dso:sprint passes `--has-tag=brainstorm:complete` in place of `--min-children=1`, and epics with the tag but zero children appear in the selectable list.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capability where sprint-list-epics.sh supports filtering by tag and includes tag data in index, enabling specific selection behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When /dso:sprint (no args) produces its hidden-epics note, the message contains the string `/dso:brainstorm` and directs the practitioner to run it on untagged epics (replacing the current \"0 children\" wording).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable behavioral property of the /dso:sprint command's output message that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A one-shot migration phase inside plugins/dso/scripts/update-artifacts.sh (invoked by the existing `dso update-artifacts` shim) iterates every open epic via the ticket reducer, greps each for the `### Planning Intelligence Log` heading in description AND comment event bodies, writes the tag for matches using read-merge-write, and prints one `UNMATCHED: <epic-id>` line to stdout per epic without a PIL match; exit code is 0 on successful completion regardless of unmatched count.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time migration script execution with completion conditions and exit behavior, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Running the migration twice against the same .tickets-tracker/ state produces identical tag state and identical `UNMATCHED:` stdout output. Marker `.claude/.brainstorm-tag-migration-v1` makes the second run a no-op exit 0. Migration is tag-only and self-guards against execution in the plugin source repo (no-op exit with a logged notice).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system properties of the migration tool's idempotent behavior and self-guarding mechanisms that persist after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When /dso:brainstorm is invoked with no arguments, its epic-selection list surfaces open epics that have children but lack the `brainstorm:complete` tag (the scrutiny-gap set) as high-value brainstorm candidates alongside the existing zero-child list.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior of the /dso:brainstorm command that will persist after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Against a fixture mixing PIL-bearing and PIL-absent open epics, the end-to-end flow verifies: (a) migration tags exactly the PIL-bearing set and reports the PIL-absent set via `UNMATCHED:` lines; (b) sprint-list-epics.sh `--has-tag=brainstorm:complete` output matches the tagged set; (c) /dso:sprint (no args) displays only the tagged set and its hidden-epics note contains `/dso:brainstorm`.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time verification task completed against test fixtures to validate migration correctness, not an ongoing system behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
